According to a report by Intel Market Research, Global Ground Based Augmentation Systems market size was valued at USD 0.85 billion in 2025. The market reaches USD 0.92 billion in 2026 and climbs to USD 1.45 billion by 2034, reflecting a CAGR of 6.1 % during the forecast period.
Ground Based Augmentation Systems are terrestrial infrastructures that enhance satellite navigation signals by providing correction data and integrity monitoring. These systems include Satellite Based Augmentation System (SBAS) ground stations, Ground Based Augmentation System (GBAS) localizers at airports, and networked reference stations that broadcast differential corrections via VHF or LTE links.
